1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,452
Lately, our Codex allowance has been disappearing fast.

2
00:00:03,452 --> 00:00:09,282
On our two-hundred-dollar monthly subscription, we've sometimes used a week's allowance in a day.

3
00:00:09,282 --> 00:00:14,280
But the remaining percentage doesn't tell us which conversations used the most.

4
00:00:14,703 --> 00:00:19,369
So I built this plugin to show usage for each conversation.

5
00:00:19,369 --> 00:00:24,460
Input, output, and the input cache share are visible without expanding anything.

6
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,701
Cache shows the percentage of input tokens read from cache.

7
00:00:28,701 --> 00:00:32,943
Expand the row for usage and cache share by model.

8
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:37,154
I wanted it easy to glance at without getting in the way.

9
00:00:37,154 --> 00:00:39,676
The window stays small, tucked into a corner.

10
00:00:39,676 --> 00:00:44,090
When you don't need it, hide it in the menu bar or system tray.

11
00:00:44,537 --> 00:00:50,083
Weekly allowance, the next automatic reset, and available manual resets are all visible.

12
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:54,350
You can also see when your next reset credit expires.

13
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:57,337
That expiry is not an automatic refill.

14
00:00:57,337 --> 00:01:01,177
It helps you plan your usage at a glance.

15
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:04,114
I also connected Tibo's X updates.

16
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:12,426
A paired Chrome extension reads his latest three original posts and flags possible reset signals and any timing he mentions.

17
00:01:12,426 --> 00:01:14,920
It's a heads-up, not a guarantee.

18
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:18,660
Your account's allowance is still the source of truth.

19
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,077
The plugin is free and open source.

20
00:01:22,077 --> 00:01:27,146
Give it a try, and let me know what could be better.

21
00:01:27,146 --> 00:01:29,680
Feedback and suggestions are always welcome.
